---
import Legal from '../../components/Legal.astro'

const toc: [string, string][] = [
  ['t1', 'Using Tolkmeet'],
  ['t2', 'Accounts'],
  ['t3', 'Plans and billing'],
  ['t4', 'Cancelling and refunds'],
  ['t5', 'Fair use'],
  ['t6', 'Translation accuracy'],
  ['t7', 'Your content'],
  ['t8', 'Open source'],
  ['t9', 'Availability'],
  ['t10', 'Ending the agreement'],
  ['t11', 'Liability'],
  ['t12', 'Governing law and contact'],
]
---
<Legal
  page="terms"
  title="Terms of Service"
  metaTitle="Terms of Service · Tolkmeet"
  metaDescription="The terms for using Tolkmeet: paid plans that renew automatically, cancel any time, and AI translations you should check for anything important."
  updated="Last updated October 17, 2026"
  toc={toc}
>
  <section class="legal-summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Tolkmeet is a paid monthly subscription.</li>
      <li>Plans renew automatically. You can cancel any time, and you keep access until the end of the period you paid for.</li>
      <li>Translations are made by AI and can be wrong. Check anything important with a qualified person.</li>
      <li>Guests you invite do not need an account, but they use Tolkmeet under these terms too.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <h2 id="t1">1. Using Tolkmeet</h2>
  <p>These terms are an agreement between you and <span lang="ko">휘슬리</span> (“we”). By creating an account or joining a meeting, you accept them. If you use Tolkmeet for an organization, you confirm you may accept these terms on its behalf.</p>

  <h2 id="t2">2. Accounts</h2>
  <p>You need an account to create meetings. Keep your sign-in details secure and tell us at support@tolkmeet.com if you suspect misuse. You are responsible for meetings created from your account, including the guests you let in.</p>

  <h2 id="t3">3. Plans and billing</h2>
  <p>Paddle.com is our merchant of record and sells Tolkmeet to you. Paddle handles payment, invoices, sales tax and VAT, under its own buyer terms.</p>
  <p>Each plan includes a number of translated meeting hours per month. Unused hours do not carry over. You can buy extra hours, which stay on your account until you use them. Prices may change; we will tell you at least 30 days before a change applies to your next renewal.</p>

  <h2 id="t4">4. Cancelling and refunds</h2>
  <p>Cancel any time from account settings; your plan stays active until the end of the paid period. Refunds follow our <a href="/refund/">Refund Policy</a> and any rights you have under consumer law where you live.</p>

  <h2 id="t5">5. Fair use</h2>
  <p>Do not use Tolkmeet to break the law, to record or translate people without the consent the law requires, to harass anyone, or to attack, overload or reverse-engineer the service beyond what the open-source license allows.</p>
  <p>We may limit or suspend accounts that put the service or other users at risk, and will tell you why unless the law prevents us.</p>

  <h2 id="t6">6. Translation accuracy</h2>
  <p>Speech recognition and translation are produced automatically by AI. They can contain errors, omissions or wrong tone. Tolkmeet is not a certified interpreter. For contracts, medical, legal or financial decisions, confirm the meaning with a qualified professional.</p>

  <h2 id="t7">7. Your content</h2>
  <p>What you say in meetings belongs to you. We process it only to provide transcription and translation, as described in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, and we do not store it.</p>

  <h2 id="t8">8. Open source</h2>
  <p>Tolkmeet’s source code is available under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0. These terms cover the hosted service at tolkmeet.com; the license covers the code.</p>

  <h2 id="t9">9. Availability</h2>
  <p>We work to keep Tolkmeet running but cannot promise it will always be available or error-free. It depends on your network, your browser and third-party services such as Google Gemini.</p>

  <h2 id="t10">10. Ending the agreement</h2>
  <p>You can close your account at any time. We may end this agreement with 30 days’ notice, or immediately for a serious breach of these terms. If we end it without cause, we refund the unused part of your prepaid plan.</p>

  <h2 id="t11">11. Liability</h2>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, and our total liability is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited by law.</p>

  <h2 id="t12">12. Governing law and contact</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Korea, without limiting mandatory consumer protections where you live. Contact: <span lang="ko">휘슬리</span> (representative: <span lang="ko">박혜연</span>, business registration number 155-03-03588), <span lang="ko">서울특별시 구로구 구일로4길 65</span>, Republic of Korea, support@tolkmeet.com.</p>
</Legal>
